            "question": "What is the difference between 157A and 200A?",
            "answer": "<p>157A is the maximum continuous charge/discharge value used for normal system sizing. 200A is the BMS protection threshold, not a continuous operating rating. Use 63A as the recommended charge-current reference and size every system component to its lowest limit.</p>"
